education is designed for content that

00:30:39.720 --> 00:30:45.400
is supposed to be shown in a classroom,

00:30:43.120 --> 00:30:47.320
right? So, content that is exclusively

00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:49.120
shown in a classroom and only in a

00:30:47.320 --> 00:30:51.080
classroom. So, unless your content is

00:30:49.120 --> 00:30:53.760
designed to exclusively and only be

00:30:51.080 --> 00:30:55.720
shown in a classroom, do not enable

00:30:53.760 --> 00:30:57.720
player for education. My brother enabled

00:30:55.720 --> 00:31:01.400
it, his channel absolutely crashed. His

00:30:57.720 --> 00:31:03.080
CPM actually shrank by about 60% when he

00:31:01.400 --> 00:31:04.120
enabled player for education. Because if

00:31:03.080 --> 00:31:05.040
you think about it, in a classroom

00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:06.760
there's probably not going to be that

00:31:05.040 --> 00:31:08.200
many ads. The ads that are shown are

00:31:06.760 --> 00:31:09.400
going to be extremely limited, and so

00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:11.080
you're just not going to make nearly as

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:12.360
much money from the video. And YouTube

00:31:11.080 --> 00:31:14.200
is probably not going to promote it as

00:31:12.360 --> 00:31:15.960
much, either. So, do not turn on player

00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:18.520
for education unless your content is

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:20.400
specifically and only designed to be

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:22.160
shown in a classroom. Now, the next tip

00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:24.440
is for most channels, but not all

00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:26.360
channels. I recommend that when you

00:31:24.440 --> 00:31:28.520
upload a video to YouTube, first of all,

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:30.120
you should be batch making your videos,

00:31:28.520 --> 00:31:31.640
and so you should always be ahead by

00:31:30.120 --> 00:31:33.680
like a week or two if you're a normal

00:31:31.640 --> 00:31:35.400
channel. But when you upload your video

00:31:33.680 --> 00:31:38.560
to YouTube, you should let it sit for

00:31:35.400 --> 00:31:40.280
about 24 to 48 hours, especially if

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:41.400
you're a beginner YouTuber. Especially

00:31:40.280 --> 00:31:44.240
if you have a new channel, because

00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:45.880
again, YouTube has so much AI slop being

00:31:44.240 --> 00:31:47.600
uploaded to the platform that they don't

00:31:45.880 --> 00:31:49.360
know who to trust. They don't know which

00:31:47.600 --> 00:31:52.640
channels to trust, and you want to give

00:31:49.360 --> 00:31:54.880
the YouTube AI 24 to 48 hours to kind of

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:56.720
scan your video or crawl your video to

00:31:54.880 --> 00:31:58.520
make sure that it's actually quality

00:31:56.720 --> 00:32:00.240
content and it's a real person. If you

00:31:58.520 --> 00:32:01.960
don't do this, if you publish your video

00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:03.920
right away, YouTube is going to have a

00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:05.560
lower trust score for your video. Now,

00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:07.760
the exception to this is if you make

00:32:05.560 --> 00:32:09.640
like news style content. Content where

00:32:07.760 --> 00:32:11.600
you need to get your content out there

00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:13.040
extremely fast because you're covering

00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:14.640
things that are happening in real time.

00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:16.320
So, if you have a news channel or you're

00:32:14.640 --> 00:32:17.800
putting recordings of some type of game,

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:18.880
you're reacting to a game that just

00:32:17.800 --> 00:32:21.320
happened or something like that,

00:32:18.880 --> 00:32:22.840
obviously don't let it sit for 24 to 48

00:32:21.320 --> 00:32:24.160
hours, that would be the exception to

00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:25.480
the rule. But for any other type of

00:32:24.160 --> 00:32:27.840
content, you might as well just let it

00:32:25.480 --> 00:32:29.800
sit for 24 to 48 hours, cuz why not?

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:31.520
It's only going to help you. Plus, you

00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:33.120
should be making content ahead of time

00:32:31.520 --> 00:32:35.200
and be one to two weeks ahead at any

00:32:33.120 --> 00:32:37.560
given time, anyways. Now, the last thing

00:32:35.200 --> 00:32:40.120
you absolutely need to do is to deep

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:41.640
link your video on playlists. So, we

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:43.600
already talked about playlists a little

00:32:41.640 --> 00:32:45.960
bit, but basically at the end of your

00:32:43.600 --> 00:32:48.200
video, you should almost always be

00:32:45.960 --> 00:32:49.840
telling people to watch another video. I

00:32:48.200 --> 00:32:51.600
do it at the end of all of my videos.

00:32:49.840 --> 00:32:53.560
All the top YouTubers do this as well.

00:32:51.600 --> 00:32:55.800
Because one of YouTube's biggest goals

00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:57.640
is to keep people on the platform. And

00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:59.680
you want them to continue to be on the

00:32:57.640 --> 00:33:01.200
platform and preferably you want them to

00:32:59.680 --> 00:33:03.640
binge watch your content. And so, I

00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:05.400
always link one of my videos at the end

00:33:03.640 --> 00:33:07.120
of every single one of my videos. I'll

00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:09.440
like say, "Click right here." And one

00:33:07.120 --> 00:33:10.920
thing that's especially helpful if

00:33:09.440 --> 00:33:13.520
you're a newbie, if you haven't had that

00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:15.240
many videos, is to deep link it inside

00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:17.560
of a playlist that you're going to be

00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:19.200
adding more videos to in the future. And

00:33:17.560 --> 00:33:21.520
so, you can do that by going to the

00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:23.720
editor and you can do that by editing

00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:25.600
the end screen. So, you want that end

00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:28.040
screen to be edited and you want to

00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:31.200
actually add element here and then you

00:33:28.040 --> 00:33:33.200
want to link it to a playlist, right?

00:33:31.200 --> 00:33:34.560
And you can link it to a video, but if

00:33:33.200 --> 00:33:37.360
you link it to a video, what you want to

00:33:34.560 --> 00:33:39.400
do is go choose specific video and then

00:33:37.360 --> 00:33:41.120
you'd want to actually find the

00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:42.960
playlist, right? So, you can see right

00:33:41.120 --> 00:33:45.200
here, this is my Coursera certificate

00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:46.760
playlist right here. And you can see all

00:33:45.200 --> 00:33:49.320
of these videos. When I click on that

00:33:46.760 --> 00:33:51.320
playlist, all of these videos are on the

00:33:49.320 --> 00:33:53.080
side. So, if I were to go to sleep, it

00:33:51.320 --> 00:33:54.280
would just cycle through all of these

00:33:53.080 --> 00:33:55.960
videos. It would play for like, you

00:33:54.280 --> 00:33:58.400
know, 10 hours straight. So, you want to

00:33:55.960 --> 00:34:00.040
find that playlist, go to edit, then you

00:33:58.400 --> 00:34:01.600
want to go to the video that you

00:34:00.040 --> 00:34:03.120
actually want to link. So, you would,

00:34:01.600 --> 00:34:05.120
you know, maybe data analytics for

00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:06.720
instance, right? And that is the one

00:34:05.120 --> 00:34:08.399
that you would add here, okay? So, you

00:34:06.720 --> 00:34:09.720
could do that or you can do a playlist

00:34:08.399 --> 00:34:10.800
and then just put your, you know, your

00:34:09.720 --> 00:34:12.240
favorite video at the top of the

00:34:10.800 --> 00:34:13.399
playlist. But the important thing is

00:34:12.240 --> 00:34:14.800
it's something that people would

00:34:13.399 --> 00:34:16.639
actually be interested in. So, that

00:34:14.800 --> 00:34:18.280
example that I used of the Coursera

00:34:16.639 --> 00:34:20.240
certificates would actually be terrible

00:34:18.280 --> 00:34:23.040
for this video. I should very likely

00:34:20.240 --> 00:34:24.280
link a Shane Hummus YouTube playlist.

00:34:23.040 --> 00:34:25.840
But if you don't want to get super fancy

00:34:24.280 --> 00:34:28.200
with the playlist, at the very least

00:34:25.840 --> 00:34:30.560
just go ahead and add a video at the

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:31.800
very end. And when you choose that video

00:34:30.560 --> 00:34:33.760
and when you put the video in the

00:34:31.800 --> 00:34:35.600
playlist as well, you want to make sure

00:34:33.760 --> 00:34:37.639
that it's a video that they're likely to

00:34:35.600 --> 00:34:39.200
want to watch. So, just as an example, I

00:34:37.639 --> 00:34:40.360
have a bunch of different topics I talk

00:34:39.200 --> 00:34:41.879
about on this channel. I talk about

00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:43.280
remote jobs sometimes, I talk about

00:34:41.879 --> 00:34:45.200
certifications, all kinds of different

00:34:43.280 --> 00:34:47.440
stuff. This is a YouTube video right

00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:49.639
here. So, I wouldn't want to link a

00:34:47.440 --> 00:34:51.560
college degree or a certification or a

00:34:49.639 --> 00:34:53.639
remote job video at the end. I would

00:34:51.560 --> 00:34:55.960
want to put it in a playlist that only

00:34:53.639 --> 00:34:57.880
has YouTube related topics, and I would

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:59.280
want to link a YouTube related topic to

00:34:57.880 --> 00:35:00.880
this video. And that is going to help

00:34:59.280 --> 00:35:02.880
you out tremendously if you do that.

00:35:00.880 --> 00:35:05.000
Now, let's talk about right when the

00:35:02.880 --> 00:35:06.560
video publishes. So, this video isn't

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:08.520
publishing yet, so I can't use this one

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:10.000
as an example, but right when the video

00:35:08.520 --> 00:35:11.800
publishes, the first thing you want to

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:14.040
do, literally the minute it publishes,

00:35:11.800 --> 00:35:16.200
is you want to comment on the video, a

00:35:14.040 --> 00:35:18.040
pinned comment. Now, you'll see in all

00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:19.720
of my videos, I have a pinned comment,

00:35:18.040 --> 00:35:21.400
and on this pinned comment, I basically

00:35:19.720 --> 00:35:23.360
promote the same exact stuff that I put

00:35:21.400 --> 00:35:25.680
at the very top of the video

00:35:23.360 --> 00:35:27.240
description. So, yeah, not everyone

00:35:25.680 --> 00:35:28.960
reads the description, but almost

00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:30.360
everyone is going to read the pinned

00:35:28.960 --> 00:35:32.000
comment. So, you want to comment this,

00:35:30.360 --> 00:35:33.920
and then you want to pin it at the very

00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:35.560
top. Additionally, there are some

00:35:33.920 --> 00:35:37.080
strategies that you can use to get

00:35:35.560 --> 00:35:38.840
engagement on the video, where you can

00:35:37.080 --> 00:35:40.000
kind of comment something clever, and

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:41.360
then a bunch of people will comment

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.960
under it, and it'll get more comments

00:35:41.360 --> 00:35:44.360
and engagement. I did that a little bit

00:35:42.960 --> 00:35:45.960
when I first started on YouTube. I don't

00:35:44.360 --> 00:35:47.640
think it's that important. Additionally,

00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:50.120
something else that you want to do is

00:35:47.640 --> 00:35:51.480
promote your video on the community tab.

00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:53.280
So, it used to be called the community

00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:54.600
tab, but now if you go to any channel,

00:35:53.280 --> 00:35:57.520
you'll see this right here. It says

00:35:54.600 --> 00:36:00.240
posts, and you can post an update to

00:35:57.520 --> 00:36:01.520
your fans. So, it's as simple as just

00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:03.120
maybe taking a little bit of the

00:36:01.520 --> 00:36:04.800
thumbnail of the video, putting that

00:36:03.120 --> 00:36:06.760
thumbnail as the image, putting the

00:36:04.800 --> 00:36:08.280
title in there, and then telling people

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:10.000
about it, and giving them a link to

00:36:08.280 --> 00:36:11.480
click on the video. It's super super

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:13.120
simple. Now, this is super effective,

00:36:11.480 --> 00:36:14.960
especially for smaller channels. You

00:36:13.120 --> 00:36:16.560
know, obviously, you can't use it until

00:36:14.960 --> 00:36:18.040
a certain point of your channel growth,

00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:19.560
but after you can use it, this is super

00:36:18.040 --> 00:36:21.320
effective to get other people to watch

00:36:19.560 --> 00:36:22.880
your content. Additionally, if you have

00:36:21.320 --> 00:36:25.200
a second channel, you can promote a

00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:26.440
smaller channel that you have, or if you

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:27.840
have friends that are bigger on YouTube,

00:36:26.440 --> 00:36:29.200
they can promote you in their community

00:36:27.840 --> 00:36:30.440
tab. You know, once in a while, for

00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:31.760
instance, I'll promote some of my

00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:33.520
students or clients if I think there's

00:36:31.760 --> 00:36:34.720
good synergy between our channels. So,

00:36:33.520 --> 00:36:36.000
attend the live training if you want to

00:36:34.720 --> 00:36:37.120
potentially become a student, click the

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:39.240
link in the description and pin comment

00:36:37.120 --> 00:36:40.920
below. But, yeah, community tab right

00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:42.680
when the video's posted can be super

00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:44.240
super useful as well because that will

00:36:42.680 --> 00:36:46.040
get more people to come to the video

00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:48.480
right when it's posted. Another tip is

00:36:46.040 --> 00:36:50.480
to respond to comments right when you

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:52.040
first upload the video. So, now I don't

00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:53.320
do the community tab anymore, but I did

00:36:52.040 --> 00:36:55.040
it when I was a smaller channel, but it

00:36:53.320 --> 00:36:56.120
just doesn't make sense for me to do it

00:36:55.040 --> 00:36:58.000
anymore as a bigger channel cuz I

00:36:56.120 --> 00:36:59.840
already get massive amounts of views and

00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:01.520
I want to send people to other

00:36:59.840 --> 00:37:03.040
platforms, right? I might want to send

00:37:01.520 --> 00:37:04.600
them to my email list or something like

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:06.200
that. So, I don't do the community tab

00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:08.720
anymore. It doesn't make sense to do it.

00:37:06.200 --> 00:37:11.360
Additionally, you do typically want to

00:37:08.720 --> 00:37:13.920
post the video at around the peak

00:37:11.360 --> 00:37:15.360
viewing time or an hour to 2 hours after

00:37:13.920 --> 00:37:17.640
the peak viewing time on your channel.

00:37:15.360 --> 00:37:19.040
Of course, you have to actually upload

00:37:17.640 --> 00:37:20.880
to your channel for a while before you

00:37:19.040 --> 00:37:22.040
can actually see the peak viewing time

00:37:20.880 --> 00:37:23.280
and you'd have to go to your audience

00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:25.640
tab to see that. But, generally

00:37:23.280 --> 00:37:27.200
speaking, afternoon in the United States

00:37:25.640 --> 00:37:28.880
is typically a good time if your

00:37:27.200 --> 00:37:30.280
audience is in the US. Some people

00:37:28.880 --> 00:37:32.120
really like the morning as well. So,

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:34.560
yeah, responding to comments right when

00:37:32.120 --> 00:37:36.160
the video is uploaded is amazing. Now,

00:37:34.560 --> 00:37:37.840
on a channel like mine, there's just way

00:37:36.160 --> 00:37:39.440
too many comments to respond to. When I

00:37:37.840 --> 00:37:40.680
had a smaller channel, I responded to

00:37:39.440 --> 00:37:42.160
every single comment. And then

00:37:40.680 --> 00:37:44.120
eventually the comments became too much,

00:37:42.160 --> 00:37:46.520
so I started only responding in the

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:48.080
first hour after I uploaded a video. And

00:37:46.520 --> 00:37:49.720
I've continued doing that for quite some

00:37:48.080 --> 00:37:52.280
time now. So, basically a lot of people

00:37:49.720 --> 00:37:54.440
know that I will respond if they comment

00:37:52.280 --> 00:37:56.080
right away on my videos. And it's almost

00:37:54.440 --> 00:37:57.960
like a little event or party in the

00:37:56.080 --> 00:37:59.680
comment section. And again, this boosts

00:37:57.960 --> 00:38:01.240
the algorithm, it boosts engagement, and

00:37:59.680 --> 00:38:03.200
it gets more people to watch your videos

00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:04.840
for longer, which is a positive sign and

00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:06.280
it gives your video the best chance of

00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:07.520
succeeding. Now, you don't absolutely

00:38:06.280 --> 00:38:08.720
have to do it, but it's something that

00:38:07.520 --> 00:38:10.400
I've done and it is something that I

00:38:08.720 --> 00:38:12.120
recommend. You could also hire somebody

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:14.760
else to do it for you, to be fair. Okay,

